# Assembly Architecture

Runtime code has three roles with **one-way references**, enforced by asmdefs or, in a single-assembly project, by review:

| Role | Contains | May reference |
|------|----------|---------------|
| **Infrastructure** | Singleton base, catalog loading, static-reset hub, shared helpers | Unity engine, `MonkeyTilt.Foundation`, `MonkeyTilt.Shared.AssetCatalog` |
| **Game state** | Client game state, server sync, session flow, player commands, wire DTOs (`Contracts/`) | Infrastructure — **never** presentation |
| **Presentation** | Scene views, HUD, overlays, input raycasts, animation, audio playback | Infrastructure and game state |

**Direction:** Presentation → Game state → Infrastructure. Never the reverse. Game state has no `Canvas`, TMP, view classes, or scene presentation code, and never spawns presentation objects — presentation bootstraps itself and subscribes.

The **folder and assembly names** that realise these roles are defined per project in its `AGENTS.md`. Do not assume `Core/`, `Gameplay/`, `Presentation/` or any other layout; read the project map first, and place a new script where that map says.

## Communication pattern

```csharp
// Presentation sends input
GameState.Instance.PlayCard(cardId, color);

// Game state notifies presentation (subscribe in OnEnable, unsubscribe in OnDisable)
GameState.Instance.HandChanged += RefreshHand;
```

Game state exposes data and events; presentation reads them in handlers. No callbacks from game state into presentation types, no presentation type names in game-state code.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — game state reaching into a view
public void OnRoundEnded() { _resultBanner.Show(_payout); }

// ✅ GOOD — game state raises an event; the banner subscribes
public event Action<decimal> RoundEnded;
```

## Namespaces match assemblies

Every script sits in the namespace its project assigns to that assembly and folder (see the project's `AGENTS.md`); no script is in the global namespace. `using` directives go outside the namespace block.

## Agent checklist

- [ ] Project `AGENTS.md` read; new script placed where its folder map says
- [ ] No presentation type referenced from game-state or infrastructure code
- [ ] Presentation communicates via game-state events and command methods only
- [ ] Namespace matches the project's assembly/folder convention; nothing in the global namespace
